Class Descriptions
⦁	ProgramMemory
	The ProgramMemory class is responsible for managing the memory used by the 	interpreter. It provides mechanisms to allocate, deallocate, and retrieve memory 	blocks used for variables, arrays, or other types of data in the program.

Public Methods:
⦁	ProgramMemory()
Constructor: Initializes the memory storage with default settings.
⦁	allocate(size_t size)
Description: Allocates a block of memory of the given size.
⦁	deallocate(void* pointer)
Description: Deallocates a previously allocated block of memory.
⦁	getMemoryUsage() const
Description: Returns the current memory usage.
⦁	clearMemory()
Description: Clears all allocated memory, ensuring that the storage is freed.

Internal Data Members:
⦁	std::vector<uint8_t> memory
Holds the allocated memory for the program. Each byte represents a unit of memory, and this data structure supports dynamic resizing.
⦁	size_t memorySize
Tracks the current size of the allocated memory.
⦁	size_t usedMemory
Tracks the amount of memory that is currently in use.

